DISCLOSURE 1, WHY THIS BUNDLE EXISTS. It pays four debts recorded during P1 and marked owed. Recording a finding is not scheduling it; leaving them as ledger entries was deferral with a citation attached. The user ruled no deferrals, and this bundle is that ruling applied. P2.1 follows.

DISCLOSURE 2, THE AUTHORITY'S BRIEF CARRIED A LOAD-BEARING FALSE PREMISE. It asserted a shared wrapper every command goes through. Measured: review, doctor and the root use defineCommand directly. Shipping the unknown-argument check only in defineGraceCommand would have left the exact surfaces F76 cited as its own example unchecked - a feature that does not fix its motivating case. The executor refuted it and the spec converts them. That premise came from a subagent survey the authority passed through as fact rather than marking for verification.

DISCLOSURE 3, TWO AUTHORITY FINDINGS WERE CORRECTED BEFORE APPROVAL. F74.1: the owed-audit list named eight tokens when 30 of 31 were locally defined; D15 is the only genuinely foreign one and was not named, and D12 is defined in BOTH plans so a bare citation resolves confidently wrong rather than dangling. F71.1: getModulePath feeds four display strings, not the two F71 named, and the live tree cannot express the defect at all because M-SKILLS has no Path AND no linked files - a criterion pointed at it passes at HEAD.

DISCLOSURE 4, AN AUTHORITY RULING FOLDED INTO THE PLAN BEFORE APPROVAL. The executor disclosed that citty renderUsage emits ANSI and that NO_COLOR is the caller's environment. Both measured. Ruling: strip the escapes before appending usage to the error message, because one string feeds both channels and the JSON envelope is a machine surface. Stripping is a transform of the single usage string, not the second rendering the executor rightly refused.

DISCLOSURE 5, RECORDED AS F78 AND SHARPER THAN ANYONE FRAMED IT. The spec, the plan and the dispatch all described the parent-run hazard as a naive check rejecting a valid command. Forcing the skip off showed otherwise: the child command SUCCEEDED, printed its JSON, and the parent then set exit 1 naming a flag the child owns. That is success-then-fail after side effects, not rejection - a caller reading the exit concludes the work did not happen while stdout says it did. It is also why the skip cannot be a hand list; it derives from the live subCommands object, verified at src/query/command.ts:217-226.

DISCLOSURE 6, THE EXECUTOR WAS WRONG ON ONE POINT AND THE AUTHORITY CHECKED. It reported the spec and plan as contradicting on D5.2, same act opposite verbs. Measured: the spec's own parenthetical reads that this is not an artifact grammar break and does not bump NGRACE_ARTIFACT_VERSION - the identical conclusion the plan states. No contradiction and no version was bumped. The binding-list phrasing that names a decision before explaining it does not force its usual consequence is legible enough to be misread by a careful reader, which is worth knowing but is not a defect.

DISCLOSURE 7, A TEST THAT COULD NOT OBSERVE ITS OWN SUBJECT. citty suppresses colour under TEST and CI as well as NO_COLOR, so under the default bun-test environment the JSON-no-escape assertion would have passed whether or not the strip existed. The executor ran it in a colour-capable child environment instead. A green that the harness guarantees is not evidence.

DISCLOSURE 8, PINS RE-MEASURED NOT FROZEN. Boolean sites 25 unmoved (no new boolean). F51 lines 806 unmoved, bytes 55043 to 55106 after three plan-id prefixes - raised to the measured value, not cut. D13 key set, the four absence codes, the live-invocation walker and package.json 6.2.0 all re-measured unmoved. F77's N is no longer pinned at 1: completeness requires N plus M to equal the inventory, so freezing N would reintroduce the under-count this debt exists to remove.

DISCLOSURE 9, REMAINING DEBT NAMED AND BEING DISCHARGED IMMEDIATELY, NOT DEFERRED. F74.1's plan-file half - qualifying D15, D12 and D5 inside docs/plans - was a NonGoal here only because bundles cannot write to docs/plans by design. It is the authority's surface and is being qualified directly after this archive, in the same session. F77's evaluator instrumentation remains a re-spec rather than a repair, and the shipped guard now fails on addition, which was the point.

DISCLOSURE 10. decisions.md was written during the open window - F74.1 and F71.1 before execution, F78 mid-window, each in its own commit ahead of the implementation commit. decisions.md is outside every bundle's ObservedWriteScope by design, and the scope audit reads working-tree porcelain, so committing removed those edits from the audit's view rather than clearing them.</Verdict></Verdicts><Decisions><Decision gate="apply" decision="permit"><Requirement id="plan-present" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">status=approved</Requirement><Requirement id="no-unresolved-satisfied-ac-clarification" required="true" present="true" blocking="false" /><Requirement id="review-verdict" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">outcome=pass</Requirement></Decision><Decision gate="archive" decision="permit"><Requirement id="no-open-epoch" required="true" present="true" blocking="false">run/ empty</Requirement></Decision></Decisions></C-RECORDED-DEBT></NgraceRunLedger>
